From ac96ea374255dc2c45c49e9e5a5b7fdf2bf06059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:57:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][PlayerInfo] The content type that the display is
 told, in the output of the Video page

A row "Content type" in the "Video output" column of the Video page, where
the connector has DRM's "content type": what the AVI InfoFrame tells the
display, as each driver makes it of the value of the property
(CONTENT_TYPE::AviOf(), hades.out.content): Cinema, Game, Photo, Computer
graphics (ITC 1, CN 0: what NVIDIA and AMD say by themselves) or Not said
(ITC 0: Intel's own, and every driver with native Dolby Vision that the TV
processes). It is what a TV with Filmmaker Mode Auto Start goes by, so that
whoever turned that on sees whether a film was said to be one. Estuary's
strings in English and Spanish; system/hades made again by make-playerinfo.py.
---
